[size=5][b][color=#E8C88A]Style Without Sacrifice - Your Transmogrification Wardrobe[/color][/b][/size]
<br />
<br />Choose how your equipment looks from a dedicated Wardrobe tab located next to the Inventory tab. Keep your equipped items and their stats while putting together a different outfit.
<br />
<br />[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Choose your look[/color][/b][/size]
<br />
<br />[list]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Five categories:[/color][/b] Browse armour, legwear, gloves/wristbands, footwear and weapons.[/*]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]An inventory-style wardrobe:[/color][/b] A six-column icon grid, game fonts and key prompts, a character preview and compact equipment slots.[/*]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Item sort:[/color][/b] Player Outfits with item icons appear first, followed by NPC Outfits without icons. Each group has a heading and its own pages and is alphabetically sorted.[/*]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Collected or all looks:[/color][/b] Filter to appearances observed on your collected equipment, or browse the full appearance catalog.[/*]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Day, night and presets:[/color][/b] Choose separate day and night outfits and save three presets to reuse in either set.[/*]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Hide equipment:[/color][/b] Hide gauntlets, feet or the sheathed weapon.[/*]
<br />[/list]
<br />[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Controls[/color][/b][/size]
<br />
<br />Press [b]End[/b] or select the Wardrobe tab in the character menu. On-screen controls also work with the mouse.
<br />
<br />[list]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Move and choose:[/color][/b] Arrow keys and Enter, or the D-pad / left stick and A. D-pad Left / Right moves horizontally; Up / Down moves vertically.[/*]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Change page:[/color][/b] Page Up / Page Down, or move past the first or last item with the D-pad / left stick. Previous and Next also work with the mouse.[/*]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Change category:[/color][/b] A / D, or the left / right trigger.[/*]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Day / night preview:[/color][/b] P, or Start / Menu.[/*]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Filter and hide:[/color][/b] Y changes Collected / All Looks; F hides a supported slot. On controller, use right stick click and left stick click respectively.[/*]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Save, load and reset:[/color][/b] T / S opens the save / load dialog; R resets the displayed set. On controller, use X / Y, or hold X to reset. Escape / B closes or cancels.[/*]
<br />[/list]
<br />[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Configuration[/color][/b][/size]
<br />
<br />Mod Setting Menu provides Enabled, Wardrobe Shortcut and Logging. Choose End, F7, F8 or F9 as the shortcut. Choose Off, Error, Warning, Info or Debug. Warning is the default; Off is silent. Debug records detailed troubleshooting information in Dawnwalker/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/UE4SS.log.
<br />
<br />Personal settings and saved outfits are stored in settings.ini and wardrobe.dat inside ue4ss/Mods/WardrobeTransmog. Keep a backup of these files. Saved outfits and collected appearances are shared across your saves.
<br />
<br />[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Installation[/color][/b][/size]
<br />
<br />[list]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Vortex:[/color][/b] Install Style-Without-Sacrifice.zip through Vortex, enable it and deploy.[/*]
<br />[*][b][color=#A8D5C2]Manual:[/color][/b] Copy Data/WardrobeTransmog into The Blood of Dawnwalker/Dawnwalker/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/Mods, preserving the folder structure.[/*]
<br />[/list]
<br />[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Reporting Bugs and other issues[/color][/b][/size]
<br />
<br />If you encounter an issue, set [b]Logging[/b] to [b]Debug[/b] in this mod’s Mod Setting Menu settings, apply the change, reproduce the issue. Then start either a bug report in the Bugs tab on Nexus (preferred method for me to track things), or at least start a new thread in comments and send me [b]Dawnwalker/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/UE4SS.log[/b] from your game folder. Do not report unrelated bugs in other people's threads, please, this makes it impossible for me to track issues.
<br />
<br />
<br />
<br />[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Notes[/color][/b][/size]
<br />
<br />Collection tracking starts with equipment observed while this mod is active. NPC appearances without inventory images use category symbols. Selected weapon appearances keep their size while drawn or sheathed, with matching scabbards and character previews. Vampire claws and fists retain their own appearance. Saved weapon looks reapply after loading. The drawn weapon remains visible when its slot is hidden. Changing the day/night preview does not switch your active equipment loadout.
<br />
<br />[size=4][b][color=#E8C88A]Credits and source[/color][/b][/size]
<br />
<br />Credit to [b]RyroNZ[/b], author of [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/237]Dawnwalker Wardrobe (Transmog)[/url], for the original Wardrobe/transmog idea. [b]MIK[/b]'s [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/353]Transmog - Your Look Your Choice[/url] also inspired the feature set.
<br />
<br />[b]This mod is an independent implementation. Not a single line of code from either author's mod was copied into this project.[/b]
<br />
<br />Thanks to the RE-UE4SS, MinHook and fmt contributors, and to [b]mmarcussa[/b] for Mod Setting Menu and its provided integration helper. Third-party notices and licenses are included in the download. The game supplies its own fonts, icons and preview assets at runtime.
<br />
<br />[url=https://github.com/my-mods/style-without-sacrifice]Source code on GitHub[/url] - the original implementation is available under the MIT license.
<br />
<br />Unofficial community content.
